```
Title: PowerShell Dynamic Module Invocation Via ExportedCommands Array Index
Author: Norbert Jaśniewicz (AlphaSOC), Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
Date: 2026-10-06
Level: high
Description: Detects PowerShell processes invoked with obfuscated command lines that enumerate Microsoft.PowerShell.Utility
 exported commands and invoke cmdlets indirectly by array index. This technique is used to evade
 detections that look for explicit strings such as Invoke-RestMethod or Invoke-Expression.
MITRE Tactic: Execution
Tags: attack.execution, attack.stealth, attack.t1027.010, attack.t1059.001
Reference: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_powershell_cmdlet_invocation_via_exported_commands_array_index.yml
 False Positives:
   - Legitimate use of exported commands array indexing during PowerShell command execution (should be rare)
```
Image IN ("*\\powershell.exe", "*\\pwsh.exe") OR OriginalFileName IN ("powershell.exe", "pwsh.dll") CommandLine="*[*]*" CommandLine IN ("*Get-Module *", "*gmo *") CommandLine="*ListAvailable*" CommandLine="*Microsoft.PowerShell.Utility*" CommandLine="*ExportedCommands*" CommandLine="*Values*"